From: gt510 <gt510@localhost>
Subject: simple: route YUV-only sensors through the CAMSS PIX line, as NV12

On MSM8916 CAMSS the ISPIF source links to three RDI lines before the PIX
line, so the breadth-first search always ended on an RDI video node. For a
sensor that only outputs YUV (the SM-T550 front SR200PC20) visit *_pix
entities first: the PIX line converts to semi-planar YUV, which the Adreno
306 imports into GL, while packed UYVY from RDI fails EGLImage import and
costs GTK a CPU download + upload per frame. Raw (Bayer) sensors are
unaffected: the MSM8916 PIX line is YUV-only, so they keep RDI.

The PIX source pad defaults to 4:2:2 (*_1X16 -> NV16), which freedreno does
not import either; request the 4:2:0 variant (*_1_5X8 -> NV12) on it.

configure() treated any media bus code change along the pipeline as a Bayer
pattern change and rebuilt a Bayer format from the NV12 capture format
(<INVALID>); only do that for raw capture formats.
---
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -492,6 +492,32 @@
 	MediaEntity *video = nullptr;
 	MediaPad *sinkPad;
 
+	/*
+	 * gt510: on Qualcomm CAMSS (MSM8916) the ISPIF feeds three raw dump
+	 * (RDI) lines and one PIX line, and RDI comes first in the link order,
+	 * so the search always ended on an RDI video node. A sensor that only
+	 * outputs YUV needs the PIX line to get semi-planar NV12/NV16, the only
+	 * YUV layouts the Adreno 306 imports into GL (packed UYVY dmabufs fail
+	 * EGLImage import and fall back to a CPU download per frame). Raw
+	 * sensors keep the RDI route: the MSM8916 PIX line is YUV-only.
+	 */
+	bool preferPix = false;
+	{
+		V4L2Subdevice subdev(sensor);
+		if (!subdev.open()) {
+			V4L2Subdevice::Formats formats = subdev.formats(0);
+			preferPix = !formats.empty();
+			for (const auto &[code, sizes] : formats) {
+				/* MEDIA_BUS_FMT_* YUV codes are 0x2000-0x2fff */
+				if (code < 0x2000 || code >= 0x3000) {
+					preferPix = false;
+					break;
+				}
+			}
+			subdev.close();
+		}
+	}
+
 	queue.push({ sensor, nullptr });
 
 	while (!queue.empty()) {
